  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 808.03 Groundwater Monitoring Wells",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 808.03 Groundwater Monitoring Wells.\n\n(a) Unless the department approves alternative methods pursuant to Env-Wq 811 that are equivalent to (1) and (2) below, monitoring wells shall be designed, installed, and decommissioned in accordance with the practices described in Env-Wq 402.22.\n\n(b) Monitoring wells shall be:\n\n(1) Purged prior to sampling; and\n\n(2) Allowed to equilibrate a minimum of 2 weeks prior to sampling for compliance purposes.\n\nSource. #10998, eff 1-1-16; ss by #14571, eff 5-15-26, EXPIRES: 5-15-36 (formerly Env-Wq 808.05)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq800.html"
